<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African March trade surplus 1.98 bln rand.</title>
<headline>S.African March trade surplus 1.98 bln rand.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa recorded a trade surplus of 1.98 billion rand in March from a 451.6 million rand deficit in February, latest South African Revenue Service figures show.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast the trade balance would show a 730 million rand surplus in March.  </p>
<p>	  (Data in billions of rand - rounded)</p>
<p>			  Mar '97	     Feb '97	    Mar '96</p>
<p>Exports		 10.951		 8.831		9.186</p>
<p>Imports		  8.972		 9.283		8.533</p>
<p>Balance		  1.979		-0.452		0.653</p>
<p>Cumulative totals:  Jan-Mar '97	 Jan-Mar '96</p>
<p>Exports		 31.031		25.557</p>
<p>Imports		 28.987		24.590</p>
<p>Balance		  2.045		 0.981</p>
<p>NOTE - This data covers the total foreign trade statistics of the common customs area of South Africa, Botswana, Lesotho, Namibia and Swaziland.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom (+27 11 482-1003)</p>
